# Generated geometry (Handoff.md §4, M-1). Wavefront .obj/.mtl are PLAIN TEXT and
# must stay out of LFS — being diffable and mergeable is the entire reason this
# project generates meshes as .obj instead of exporting .glb. Do not "tidy" these
# into the LFS block below.
#
# B-84: FileAccess.store_line() always writes LF. Without eol=lf pinned here,
# a checkout with core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) converts these to
# CRLF on checkout, so every regenerate-and-diff run "changes" every line with
# zero real content difference — exactly the class of noise that makes the
# M-block's "generate twice, git status must be clean" determinism test
# unreliable. Force LF both ways regardless of the checking-out machine's
# autocrlf setting.
*.obj text eol=lf
*.mtl text eol=lf

# Same bug, same fix, found the same way — smoke gate step 1 is
# `--import && git status --short`, and on a machine with core.autocrlf=true
# (the Windows default) that step could never come back clean. Checkout writes
# these with CRLF; Godot's importer rewrites every one of them with LF the first
# time it runs; `git status` then reports all 34 as modified while
# `git diff` shows nothing and the blob hashes are identical, because the change
# is purely the line endings git is about to convert back.
#
# It is worse than cosmetic: a gate whose "no tracked churn" check always fails
# is a gate everybody learns to read past, which is how real churn gets waved
# through. Pin them the way `.obj`/`.mtl` are pinned.
*.import text eol=lf

# And the text formats Godot itself writes, for the same reason — the editor
# saves scenes, resources and scripts with LF on every platform, so anything
# opened and saved in it would churn exactly like the `.import` files did.
# These carry `text` so they still diff and merge like code, which is the whole
# reason this project keeps scenes and resources in their text formats.
*.tscn text eol=lf
*.tres text eol=lf
*.gd text eol=lf
*.gdshader text eol=lf

# Third-party licence texts — never converted, never normalised. These are
# vendored documents that Form 03 quotes verbatim; `git add --renormalize .`
# would otherwise rewrite all eight of them the first time anyone runs it, which
# is a diff nobody wants to have to justify on a submission artifact.
*LICENSE*.txt -text
*LICENCE*.txt -text

# Binary assets — track via Git LFS (run: git lfs install)
*.glb filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.gltf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.fbx filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpeg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.ttf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.otf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.wav filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mp3 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.ogg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
